28
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.760
He is an inspiration to me

29
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.880
and I think we have so much to learn from him.

30
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.740
He's so knowledgeable too,

31
00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.040
and he has great taste in movies and TV,

32
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.720
he's so well-read.

33
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.760
The award-winning, life affirming,

34
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.593
cross stitching, Jonah Larson.

35
00:01:32.823 --> 00:01:35.073
(applause)

36
00:01:35.954 --> 00:01:37.850
For the first time in two years,

37
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.440
I get to see him in person.

38
00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.640
Please welcome my dear friend, Jonah Larson.

39
00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:46.862
(applause and uplifting music)

40
00:01:56.768 --> 00:01:59.367
Oh Jonah, I'm so happy to see you.

41
00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:00.770
I'm so glad to be back.

42
00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.920
Oh my gosh. This has been such a long journey.

43
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.440
It is, and before we get started,

44
00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.180
I have to start this, I always start with

45
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.937
hello, crochet friends.

46
00:02:09.937 --> 00:02:12.187
(applause)

47
00:02:14.107 --> 00:02:17.000
What did you think about the crochet world

48
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.623
hitting the Olympics and like Olympics X crochet?

49
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.820
It was so cool to see Tom Daley,

50
00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.090
the gold medal winning diver crocheting

51
00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.870
because it really brings crochet

52
00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.390
to a whole new generation of younger folks,

53
00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.780
and it shows that it's for everyone,

54
00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.480
not just the grandma hobby it's for men

55
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.090
and everyone else included.

56
00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.980
And I think maybe crochet might even be

57
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.140
an Olympic sport one day

58
00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.199
because of the hand dexterity needed.

59
00:02:41.199 --> 00:02:43.449
(applause)

60
00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:49.110
Well, of course you know I was watching Tom Daley

61
00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.810
the whole time thinking of you,

62
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.960
and he knew that you were going to be on the show today,

63
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.130
so he has a message for you.

64
00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.363
Oh wow.

65
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.690 line:15%
Hi Jonah, it's Tom Daley here, Olympic diver,

66
00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.970 line:15%
but also fellow stitching enthusiast.

67
00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.670 line:15%
And I just wanted to say how awesome I think you are.

68
00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.273 line:15%
One, your designs are amazing, but secondly,

69
00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.100
you're just incredible and you're so fast,

70
00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.390
and able to talk at the same time

71
00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:15.800
as doing all of those stitches,

72
00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.080
and the way that you speak so eloquently about it,

73
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.270
and how much happiness and joy you bring to so many people.

74
00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.910
One day, I hope I'm going to be able to meet you

75
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.280
and we can have a real sit down and we can have a stitch.

76
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.040
I can knit, crochet, we can all have a lovely time,

77
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.860
but in the meantime, keep doing what you're doing.

78
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.480
I think you're awesome.

79
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.126
Crochet away friends.

80
00:03:33.126 --> 00:03:35.376
(applause)

81
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.420
You know, I thought it was cool

82
00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.910
when I won 20 blue ribbons on my local state fair.

83
00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.378
And now I'm rethinking that.

84
00:03:49.378 --> 00:03:51.040
(laughter)

85
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.670
That's pretty baller that Tom Daley is saying...

86
00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.940
That is super cool.

87
00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.700
Your theme, your term, crochet away.

88
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.770
Yeah, that was pretty cool, I wasn't expecting that.

89
00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.910
Okay, so a big part of who you are,

90
00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.390
you know, is that you give back to meaningful causes

91
00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.750
and recently you completed a big project in Ethiopia.

92
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.730
And can you tell us about it?

93
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.220
I'll start with the little origin story and backstories.

94
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.890
So when I was six months old,

95
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:19.080
I was adopted from a very rural area in Ethiopia that didn't

96
00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:22.580
have a library, science lab, or a school altogether, really.

97
00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:26.530
And I've been working with thousands of people,

98
00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.860
and you too, because you helped me build.

99
00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.690
And I was able to build a library that services

100
00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:34.050
over 2000 students and has 3000 books,

101
00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.770
and I've also been able to give them a science lab.

102
00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.680
And now they received an award called

103
00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.040
The Federal Medallia for Academic Excellence

104
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.288
from the Ethiopian government.

105
00:04:43.288 --> 00:04:45.538
(applause)

106
00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:54.699
I mean, Jonah, you were adopted in Ethiopia

107
00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:00.440
and like, what is it that makes you be the kind of person

108
00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.470
that says I want to give back to that community?

109
00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.140
Well, I have to give the credit to my mom

110
00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.368
over there in mint shirt because she is the one.

111
00:05:08.368 --> 00:05:10.846
There she is! Hi, how are you?

112
00:05:10.846 --> 00:05:13.096
(applause)

113
00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.410
And I heard that you also still have

114
00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.460
some big plans for the school as well.

115
00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.160
The school has received an award for academic excellence,

116
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.740
but it's still not up to hygiene standards yet.

117
00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:31.650
And they have a outhouse that doesn't meet their needs,

118
00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.720
and it's not good for those children.

119
00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.130
So right now I'm working on building

120
00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:39.380
latrines for them, so that females,

121
00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.810
they can have their privacy.

122
00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.750
So they can attend school all the time

123
00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.010
and get a good education.

124
00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.150
And you have a Go Fund Me,

125
00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.052
and you have a...

126
00:05:46.052 --> 00:05:47.030
I have a Go Fund Me in the website,

127
00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.300 line:15%
jonahhands.com and I've already raised

128
00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.090 line:15%
1500 for this part of the project,

129
00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.330 line:15%
but I still have 5,500 to go.

130
00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.019 line:15%
Okay, well thank you for bringing

131
00:05:55.019 --> 00:05:58.720
the awareness and attention to everything that you do Jonah.

132
00:05:58.720 --> 00:05:59.840
Now back to crocheting,

133
00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.730
we have a few audience members here,

134
00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.760
and I'm so excited to introduce a new segment we're calling

135
00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.860
'Crochet and A'.

136
00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.360
(harp music and applause)

137
00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.770
All righty here, we're going to go to our first question.

138
00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.820
It's to Carmen, Let's see...

139
00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.520
Carmen, there you are Carmen!

140
00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.080
Welcome to the show.

141
00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.030
Thank you, Hi Jonah, my question is,

142
00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.810
I'm trying to get my daughter into crocheting,

143
00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:29.930
to get excited to crochet with me.

144
00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.107 line:15%
Is there a go-to project that you can tell us about,

145
00:06:33.107 --> 00:06:34.430 line:15%
